    note: "Peer-reviewed study (J Hered. 2007;98(5):539-543, PMID 17586598) identifying an autosomal recessive G-to-A missense mutation (valine-to-methionine substitution) in exon 6 of the choline acetyltransferase (CHAT) gene causing congenital myasthenic syndrome ('muskeltræthed') in Old Danish Pointing Dogs and establishing a breed-specific DNA test."
